"Dark Tunnel"
"A stream of pale light filters through a narrow breach in the eastern wall of
the confined corridor, quickly fading away into the utter darkness lying
westward.  Roughly hewn, hand-carved stone form the walls of the passage,
stretching to form a low arching ceiling overhead.  Grim patches of dull green
moss have taken root in the various crevices and cracks of the pale gray rock.
The air here hangs heavy with musk and dust and the odor of dead air.
